## 1. Purpose

NOVA Skin is published as a public community preview to allow people to inspect, learn from, experiment with, and contribute to the project's community layer.

This license is intended to encourage experimentation while preserving the identity and architectural control of NOVA Skin.

## 2. Permissions

You may:

* view the source code;
* study the architecture;
* run NOVA Skin for personal use;
* install and test the extension locally;
* create personal theme variations;
* create and share compatible theme presets;
* modify community theme files for personal experimentation;
* propose improvements or contributions to the project.

## 3. Restrictions

You may not, without explicit written permission from the copyright holder:

* sell NOVA Skin or modified copies as a standalone product;
* redistribute the complete project as your own product;
* remove or alter copyright, attribution, or project identity notices;
* represent NOVA Skin as an official OpenAI product;
* use the NOVA name, branding, or identity to imply official endorsement;
* package the NOVA Skin core into another commercial product;
* use the project or its core architecture as the basis of a competing commercial skin platform.

## 4. Community themes

Themes and JSON presets created by community contributors may be shared independently when they do not include or redistribute the NOVA Skin core.

Community contributors retain ownership of their original creative work.

By submitting a contribution to the NOVA Skin project, the contributor grants NOVA permission to use, modify, display, distribute, and include that contribution as part of NOVA Skin and its community materials.

## 5. No warranty

NOVA Skin is provided for experimentation and personal use.

It is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind.

The project may require updates when the underlying ChatGPT interface changes.

